    "narrative": "With an eye toward maintaining our competitive edge in stolen bases, today\u2019s lineup prioritizes high-upside speed threats against vulnerable arms. **Gunnar Henderson** stands out as our premier start (74.74) despite the formidable presence of Cole on the mound; the 16% park factor boost and his prime #3 spot anchor the offense. Close behind, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Bradish, where his dynamic platoon split and #4 order positioning provide the offensive ceiling we need. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Heliot Ramos** (65.99) are also vital, as both utilize favorable SP matchups (Holmes and Bradish, respectively) to push well into the strong-start category, ensuring our daily efficiency remains high.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nasim Nunez** (37.98), who failed to clear the 40-point threshold solely due to the daunting task of facing deGrom. While **Nasim Nunez** provides the elite speed that usually mandates a start in our Roto format, the combination of a bottom-third order placement and the pitcher's elite skill set created a floor too low to risk, especially with the Austin Waves looking to preserve game caps. Meanwhile, **Drake Baldwin** (64.68) remains a locked-in start, as his xwOBA profile and secure #2 spot offer rare stability at the catcher position. We are currently navigating a quiet day for **Kyle Tucker**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** due to team off-days, forcing us to rely on our active core to maintain our category leads. Managers should monitor any late weather shifts, but currently, no extreme conditions threaten to derail the projected performance of **Miguel Vargas** or **Wade Meckler**.",
